---
# clang-tidy configuration for Muyo (#24).
#
# This replaces a borrowed google-cloud-cpp config whose `WarningsAsErrors: "*"` and C++14 rationale had
# never been run here (its `ConstMemberCase: UPPPER_CASE` typo made that key a no-op). The set below is
# curated from measurements on this tree, not from a preset:
#
#  * `bugprone-*` and `clang-analyzer-*` are in. They found the classes that have actually bitten this
#    repository: a null device dereference in `RenderGraphExecutor`'s constructor, size arithmetic widened
#    after a `uint32_t` multiplication (the #124 4 GiB class), and a virtual call from a destructor.
#  * `bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters` is out: two adjacent same-type parameters are often the API
#    (`Initialize(extensions, layers)`), and the check cannot distinguish the real risk from the shape.
#  * `clang-diagnostic-*` is out: those are compiler diagnostics, which GCC 13 with `-Wall -Wextra`
#    already owns; enabling clang's set here would duplicate them and add clang-only ones (28
#    `unused-private-field` findings) that belong in a cleanup pass, not behind a gate.
#  * `bugprone-switch-missing-default-case` is out: this repository uses exhaustive switches with no
#    default on purpose (a new enumerator must warn, not fall into a silent default; see `NameOf`).
#  * `bugprone-narrowing-conversions` is out until the legacy `src/RenderPasses/` findings are triaged.
#  * `clang-analyzer-optin.performance.Padding` is out: Vulkan structs are ABI-fixed and cannot be
#    reordered, so the finding is not actionable.
#  * `performance-*` is out for now: adding it to this set over the same 52 TUs produced 32 findings, 19
#    of them `performance-avoid-endl` on six files (Debug.cpp 7, VkRenderDevice.cpp 4,
#    RenderGraphExecutor.cpp 3, RenderGraphBuilder.cpp 2, helloVulkan.cpp 2, Scene.cpp 1); that `std::endl`
#    use is deliberate in the application output.
#  * `readability-*`/`modernize-*`/`cppcoreguidelines-*` are a later pass; they would produce a large
#    style diff, and this repository has its own conventions in docs/CodingConventions.md.
#
# Enforcement is staged (AGENTS.md section 5): report-only until the current findings are triaged, then
# `scripts/sanity.sh tidy` applies this set to changed lines via clang-tidy-diff with warnings as errors.
# Pin clang-tidy 18 (the version .clang-format and CI use): newer releases add checks and change results,
# so a version bump is a deliberate change with its own measurement.
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  -clang-diagnostic-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-narrowing-conversions,
  -bugprone-switch-missing-default-case,
  -clang-analyzer-optin.performance.Padding,
WarningsAsErrors: ''
# Anchored on the checkout directory name: a bare `src/` pattern also matched
# `build/_deps/catch2-src/src/...`, and the report-only gate was 30/35 vendored diagnostics. clang-tidy 18
# has no exclude-header key (that arrived later), so the repo directory is part of the anchor; a checkout
# under another name would simply report no header diagnostics rather than the wrong ones.
HeaderFilterRegex: '^.*/Muyo/src/.*\.(h|hpp|cpp)$'
SystemHeaders: false
